From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 7 Jul 2026 00:18:17 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat(hooks): model Hermes native shell hooks (correct false
 'no hook surface' matrix claim)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Cross-check finding: Hermes (NousResearch Hermes Agent) DOES have a native
hook surface — shell hooks in the `hooks:` block of the GLOBAL ~/.hermes/config.yaml,
where a pre_tool_call hook can DENY a tool call (it even accepts Claude's
{decision:block} shape). The matrix wrongly said hooks=unsupported.

- hook-renderer: add renderHermesHooksYaml() projecting protected-path +
  tdd-gate onto Hermes pre_tool_call matchers (write_file|patch, terminal);
  renderHookConfig treats hermes as global-config scope (skip, never written),
  mirroring Codex.
- adapter: read Hermes tool_input.path; emit the Hermes {action:block,message}
  block shape for --harness hermes.
- matrix: hermes hooks unsupported -> not-delivered (global-config) with
  accurate knownIssue + new source S16 (Hermes hooks doc).
- correct the false 'no documented hook mechanism' claim in the 2026-06-19
  kernel-skill-surface design doc (dated correction note).
- tests: Hermes renderer, global-config skip, adapter path + block shape.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
